Parity disposition: the web <VehicleSelect> is a drop-in <Select> wired to useSelectedVehicle(); its only
direct hook beyond that store is useTranslation (the single key vehicleSelect.aria). The native peer keeps
that contract — the host's current fleet + selection (web `vehicles` + `vehicleId`) arrive via the P1/S8
VehicleSelectSource snapshot and a chosen option routes back out through the host-supplied `onSelect` closure
(the native peer of `setVehicleId`; production wires it to the shared SelectedVehicleStore + useVehicles()
feed). Every REAL web behaviour is reproduced: the option mapping with the exact fallback chain
`display_name || vin || `Vehicle ${id}`` (empty string falsy), the controlled value
`vehicleId != null ? String(vehicleId) : ''`, the onChange parse
`Number(value); isFinite && > 0 ? n : null` (clear-to-null), and the optional leading Car glyph (`withIcon`).
The web returns `null` for an empty fleet; the P4 always-render contract reproduces that as a compact,
labelled empty indicator (never a blank box), and adds the leaf states (loading skeleton / error retry tile)
and the orthogonal freshness chip (stale auto-refresh once / offline keeps the cached fleet). The shared
@/components/ui Select maps to the native shared TSSelect. Charts/maps: NONE in source → NONE here.

